  "outcome": "O14",
  "verdict": {
    "outcome": "O14",
    "direction": "worsens",
    "magnitude": "moderate",
    "time_horizon": "this-parliament",
    "confidence": "moderate",
    "plain": "Abolishing IR35 would widen the tax gap between high-earning contractors and ordinary employees, disproportionately benefiting higher-income self-employed individuals while costing the Exchequer roughly \u00a32 billion a year \u2014 money that would otherwise fund public services used by lower earners. The main uncertainty is how much of the gain flows to genuinely low-income sole traders versus higher-earning disguised employees.",
    "biggest_unknown": "Whether lost tax revenue leads to public spending cuts or tax rises that fall on lower earners, and the degree to which the gains are concentrated among higher-earning contractors versus low-income sole traders.",
